<Docs title="Web integration" intro="Install the browser library or copy editable source into your project.">
<h2>Install for the web</h2><pre><code>npm install @austindelic/blackhole react react-dom</code></pre>
<p>Render into a container with an explicit height. The component owns its canvas and releases GPU resources when it unmounts.</p>
<pre><code>{`import { BlackHole } from '@austindelic/blackhole/react';

export function Scene() {
  return (
    <div style={{ height: '100vh', background: '#080807' }}>
      <BlackHole
        showControls={false}
        quality="cinematic-ascii"
        asciiEnabled={true}
        exposure={2}
        bloomStrength={0.65}
      />
    </div>
  );
}`}</code></pre>
<h2>Renderer options</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Use it for</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>quality</code></td><td><code>mobile-safe</code>, <code>ascii-balanced</code>, or <code>cinematic-ascii</code>. The explorer offers Desktop (<code>cinematic-ascii</code>, the default on all devices) and Low / mobile (<code>mobile-safe</code>). <code>ascii-balanced</code> remains available in the package API.</td></tr><tr><td><code>asciiEnabled</code></td><td>Switch between glyphs and raw rendered light.</td></tr><tr><td><code>exposure</code> / <code>bloomStrength</code></td><td>Adjust brightness and the glow around the accretion disk.</td></tr><tr><td><code>interactive</code></td><td>Enable pointer and keyboard camera navigation.</td></tr><tr><td><code>backend</code></td><td><code>auto</code>, <code>webgl2</code>, or <code>webgpu</code>. Support depends on the browser and device.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p>The <a href="/explore/">explorer</a> exports a JSON configuration with renderer props and a selected camera preset. Its share link stores the same settings in the URL; it does not upload them to a server.</p>
<h2>Astro and server rendering</h2><p>Mount the interactive component on the client with Astro's React integration. The page and documentation can remain static HTML.</p><pre><code>{`---
import { BlackHole } from '@austindelic/blackhole/react';
---
<div style="height: 100vh">
  <BlackHole client:only="react" showControls={false} />
</div>`}</code></pre>
<h2>Install editable source</h2><pre><code>npx @austindelic/blackhole-cli add --framework react \
  --out-dir src/blackhole</code></pre><p>The CLI writes editable renderer source into your project. Use <code>--dry-run</code> to inspect the file list first. Existing files are protected unless you explicitly request <code>--overwrite</code>.</p>
<h2>Build from source</h2><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/austindelic/blackhole.git
cd blackhole
bun install
bun run --cwd packages/blackhole build
bun run --cwd apps/explorer dev</code></pre>
<p>Source installs use the workspace package. You can inspect the shader pipeline, run the explorer locally, and propose changes without publishing anything.</p>
<h2>Performance and accessibility</h2><p>GPU support and thermal limits vary. Keep a static image available, select Low / mobile when Desktop is too demanding, and honor <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>. The explorer starts paused when reduced motion is requested and keeps its controls available if rendering fails.</p>
<p>See the <a href="https://github.com/austindelic/blackhole/blob/main/WEB_API.md">package API contract</a> for the complete supported surface.</p>
</Docs>
